{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TransferFactorCommute","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.TransferFactorCommute","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.he3_ppn_pnp_readout_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.he3_ppn_pnp_readout_eq","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L175-L182","doc":"**The ³He nucleon-level degeneracy, as a theorem.**\n\nFor a proton at position 0 the later strands of `ppn` contribute\n`d(p,p) = a` then `d(p,n) = b`, while those of `pnp` contribute them in the\nopposite order. The objective cannot tell the two arrangements apart. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout_chainProd_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout_chainProd_perm","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L169-L173","doc":"**The per-strand `Φ_q` datum depends only on the multiset of crossing\ncoefficients contributed by the strands after it.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout_transferFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout_transferFactor","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L161-L167","doc":"The readout is not a constant function of the state — so the invariance\nresults below are statements about the chain, not artefacts of a degenerate\nreadout. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.phiReadout","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L157-L159","doc":"The `Φ_q` readout of a chain state: `V̂ = z · M₁₀ + M₁₁`, mirroring\n`V_sym = z * M10 + M11`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chainProd_perm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chainProd_perm","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L146-L155","doc":"**The chain product depends on the crossing coefficients only as a\nmultiset**: permuting the later strands cannot change it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.chainProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.chainProd","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L141-L144","doc":"The chain product over a list of crossing coefficients, in list order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor_comm","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L130-L139","doc":"**Any two transfer factors of the same chain commute.**\n\nNot a triviality: the carrier is non-commutative (`M2.mulNotComm`) and the\nreadout `phiReadout` is not symmetric in the entries. Commutation holds because\nevery factor is `S + d · 1` for one and the same `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor_eq_skeleton_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor_eq_skeleton_add","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L121-L128","doc":"`T(d) = S + d · 1` componentwise — the reason the factors commute:\nthe crossing coefficient only ever adds a multiple of the identity, and never\ntouches the off-diagonal structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.transferSkeleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.transferSkeleton","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L118-L119","doc":"The `d`-independent skeleton `S = ((h, 1), (1, 0))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.transferFactor","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L114-L116","doc":"One step of the `Φ_q` transfer chain for crossing coefficient `d`:\n`T(d) = ((h + d, 1), (1, d))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.mulNotComm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.mulNotComm","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L101-L110","doc":"**The carrier is genuinely non-commutative.**\n\nGuards the commutation theorem below against vacuity: if `M2 R` were a\ncommutative monoid, `transferFactor_comm` would say nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L98-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.one_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.one_mul","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L95-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul_assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul_assoc","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L91-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.one","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The identity transfer state the chain starts from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.mul","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L81-L86","doc":"Matrix product, transcribed from the Python update\n`n00 = M00*t00 + M01*t10`, `n01 = M00*t01 + M01*t11`,\n`n10 = M10*t00 + M11*t10`, `n11 = M10*t01 + M11*t11`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.m11","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.m11","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L77-L77","doc":"entry `M₁₁` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.m10","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.m10","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L75-L75","doc":"entry `M₁₀` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.m01","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.m01","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L73-L73","doc":"entry `M₀₁` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.m00","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.m00","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L71-L71","doc":"entry `M₀₀` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.M2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.M2","kind":"structure","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/TransferFactorCommute.lean#L67-L77","doc":"The `2 × 2` transfer state of the `Φ_q` chain, carried as the four scalars\n`M00, M01, M10, M11` exactly as `_phi1_from_ordering_sym` does. ","signatureChunk":0}]}